# Local tool state — machine-specific, not shared
.tokensave/
.claude/settings.local.json
# Live pdlc consumer config is per-machine state; the tracked arrangement lives
# in .claude/pdlc.config.example.json (read by pdlc/engine's ci-arrangement test).
# Anchored so the covered-violations fixture's nested .claude/ tree is untouched.
/.claude/pdlc.config.json
.claude/.headroom_wrap_marker.json

# Node
node_modules/

# Generated consumer runtime copies — installed from pdlc/workflows/dist/ by
# pdlc/hooks/scripts/sync-workflows.sh. The leading slash is explicit-but-redundant: per
# gitignore(5), a pattern containing a separator anywhere but the trailing position is already
# relative to this .gitignore's own directory, so `.claude/workflows/` and `/.claude/workflows/`
# match identically. What must NOT be used here is a slash-free pattern (`workflows/`) or an
# explicit `**/` — either matches at every depth and would reach the checked-in
# covered-violations fixture's nested `.claude/workflows/`.
#
# What that would and would NOT do (SE G-04, Phase CR — the earlier claim here, that it turns
# AT-23's `== 7` into `== 0`, was wrong on two independent counts, both measured):
#   - It would NOT change AT-23. `listAllFiles()` in `lib/document-oracles.mjs` walks the tree
#     with `readdirSync` and never consults git, so no ignore pattern can alter what the oracle
#     sees.
#   - It would NOT untrack the fixture either. Ignore rules do not apply to already-tracked
#     paths: with a matching pattern added, the tracked files stay tracked, `git ls-files` still
#     lists them, and a fresh clone still materialises them.
# The anchoring is still right, for the reason that actually survives measurement: an unanchored
# pattern would silently make *newly added* files under the fixture's nested `.claude/workflows/`
# un-`git add`-able without `-f`, so a future fixture file would go missing at authoring time
# rather than loudly failing. Measured on git 2.50.1 (TSPEC §10.1).
/.claude/workflows/

# pdlc consolidation in-progress marker — working tree only (AC-1.3)
docs/_decisions/.consolidation-lock
